{"schema": "document.v2", "source_id": "eur-lex.europa.eu", "source_name": "EUR-Lex", "url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/oj/browse-oj.html", "canonical_url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/oj/browse-oj.html", "fetch_time": "2026-06-23T06:39:49.716366+00:00", "language": "en", "title": "Browse the Official Journal", "published_date": "2026-06-23T06:39:48.207975+00:00", "updated_date": null, "doc_type": "Blog/News", "programme": ["Other/NA"], "finance_instrument": [], "stage": null, "actors": [], "tech_area": [], "monetary_values": [], "summary_150w": "Do you want to help improving EUR-Lex ? This is a list of experimental features that you can enable. These features are still under development; they are not fully tested, and might reduce EUR-Lex stability. Don't forget to give your feedback! This document is an excerpt from the EUR-Lex website\nEU law\nEU case-law\nOfficial Journal\nNational law and case-law\nInformation\nResults 1 - 7 of 7\nResults 1 - 7 of 7\n\nReferences\n• Source — 23 Jun 2026 — https://eur-lex.europa.eu/oj/browse-oj.html", "key_points": [], "implications": {"innovation_direction": [], "capital_structure": [], "regulatory_change": []}, "links": {"pdf": [], "dataset": [], "related": []}, "celex_id": null, "call_id": null, "award_id": null, "tags": [], "dedupe_signature": "e818bad8642efedcfca2e1c2e4f3f15645c1c26ffae05b6d533d85083c931b4f", "embeddings": null, "extraction_notes": null}
{"schema": "document.v2", "source_id": "eur-lex.europa.eu", "source_name": "EUR-Lex", "url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/oj/all/auth-direct-access.html", "canonical_url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/oj/all/auth-direct-access.html", "fetch_time": "2026-06-23T06:39:51.843939+00:00", "language": "en", "title": "Official Journal - Legally binding printed editions", "published_date": "2026-06-23T06:39:50.271686+00:00", "updated_date": null, "doc_type": "Blog/News", "programme": ["Other/NA"], "finance_instrument": [], "stage": null, "actors": [], "tech_area": [], "monetary_values": [], "summary_150w": "Do you want to help improving EUR-Lex ? This is a list of experimental features that you can enable. These features are still under development; they are not fully tested, and might reduce EUR-Lex stability. Don't forget to give your feedback! This document is an excerpt from the EUR-Lex website\nEU law\nEU case-law\nOfficial Journal\nNational law and case-law\nInformation\nSince 1 July 2013 (the date Regulation No 216/2013 entered into force), only the electronic editions of the Official Journal\n   are authentic and produce legal effects. However, if the information systems are affected by an unforeseen and exceptional disruption, it may not be possible to publish\n   the electronic edition of an Official Journal on EUR-Lex. In this case, the edition concerned is published in printed form. This printed edition is authentic and produces legal effects. Since the entry into force of Regulation No 2024/741 on 14 March 2024, such printed edition is considered authentic until the systems are restored and the corresponding electronic\n   edition is made available on EUR-Lex. From that moment on, only the electronic edition is considered authentic. Three printed editions of the Official Journal had authentic status between 1 July 2013 and the entry into force of Regulation No 2024/741 . Since 14 March 2024, only the corresponding electronic editions published on EUR-Lex are considered authentic and produce\n   legal effects. Results 1 - 3 of 3\nResults 1 - 3 of 3\n\nReferences\n• Source — 23 Jun 2026 — https://eur-lex.europa.eu/oj/all/auth-direct-access.html", "key_points": [], "implications": {"innovation_direction": [], "capital_structure": [], "regulatory_change": []}, "links": {"pdf": [], "dataset": [], "related": []}, "celex_id": null, "call_id": null, "award_id": null, "tags": [], "dedupe_signature": "fec4814ebf3b9e013b48acf6ea97e933f39d1bb29800f91a5506b25e5a777f1d", "embeddings": null, "extraction_notes": null}
{"schema": "document.v2", "source_id": "eur-lex.europa.eu", "source_name": "EUR-Lex", "url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eu-enlargement/special.html", "canonical_url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eu-enlargement/special.html", "fetch_time": "2026-06-23T06:39:53.875469+00:00", "language": "en", "title": "Browse by Official Journal Special Edition", "published_date": "2026-06-23T06:39:52.392488+00:00", "updated_date": null, "doc_type": "Blog/News", "programme": ["Other/NA"], "finance_instrument": [], "stage": null, "actors": [], "tech_area": [], "monetary_values": [], "summary_150w": "Do you want to help improving EUR-Lex ? This is a list of experimental features that you can enable. These features are still under development; they are not fully tested, and might reduce EUR-Lex stability. Don't forget to give your feedback! This document is an excerpt from the EUR-Lex website\nEU law\nEU case-law\nOfficial Journal\nNational law and case-law\nInformation\nThe Special Edition of the Official Journal contains the secondary law in force on\n   the date of accession of the given Member State. Acts published in the special editions are grouped in volumes in the order of their\n   publication and are listed in 20 chapters, corresponding to the chapters of the directory\n   of European Union legislation.\n\nReferences\n• Source — 23 Jun 2026 — https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eu-enlargement/special.html", "key_points": [], "implications": {"innovation_direction": [], "capital_structure": [], "regulatory_change": []}, "links": {"pdf": [], "dataset": [], "related": []}, "celex_id": null, "call_id": null, "award_id": null, "tags": [], "dedupe_signature": "373eeab5c0d97a16ae626204a1886ca94df2e880cc27297d7c9c734b5e0c86b9", "embeddings": null, "extraction_notes": null}
{"schema": "document.v2", "source_id": "eur-lex.europa.eu", "source_name": "EUR-Lex", "url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/collection/n-law/mne.html", "canonical_url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/collection/n-law/mne.html", "fetch_time": "2026-06-23T06:39:55.799550+00:00", "language": "en", "title": "National transposition", "published_date": "2026-06-23T06:39:54.274067+00:00", "updated_date": null, "doc_type": "Blog/News", "programme": ["Other/NA"], "finance_instrument": [], "stage": null, "actors": [], "tech_area": [], "monetary_values": [], "summary_150w": "Do you want to help improving EUR-Lex ? This is a list of experimental features that you can enable. These features are still under development; they are not fully tested, and might reduce EUR-Lex stability. Don't forget to give your feedback! This document is an excerpt from the EUR-Lex website\nEU law\nEU case-law\nOfficial Journal\nNational law and case-law\nInformation\nIn this section you can find measures adopted by the EU Member States to transpose\n   EU acts – mainly directives – into national law. You can search for the titles, and,\n   if available, the texts of the measures, together with information on the dates of\n   notification, national identifiers of the acts and links to the transposed EU act. This section is updated each week. The left-hand side of this page gives access to search tools. To obtain an overview of all the national transposition measures adopted for a specific\n   directive by EU Member States, go to the page of the directive and then click “national\n   transposition” in the left-hand menu. An automatic translation tool is available to translate the title and, if available, the text of national measures into any\n   official EU language. More on national transpositions Less on national transpositions\nDirectives are EU legal acts which set binding objectives to be achieved by the EU Member States\n      to which they are addressed ( Article 288 of the Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union). Member States can choose the form and methods for transposing directives into national\n      law. However, they are bound by the terms of the directive as to the result to be\n      achieved and the deadline by which the transposition should take place. National authorities\n      must notify the European Commission of the measures they have adopted. The European\n      Commission verifies the completeness and correctness of transposition of EU law into\n      national law. EUR-Lex publishes information on national transposition measures (title, date of publication,\n      transposed directive/s, etc.). National authorities can also express their willingness\n      to make the text of national measures available on EUR-Lex. The Member States are\n      solely responsible for all information they provide on transposition of EU law into\n      national law present in this section.\n\nReferences\n• Source — 23 Jun 2026 — https://eur-lex.europa.eu/collection/n-law/mne.html", "key_points": [], "implications": {"innovation_direction": [], "capital_structure": [], "regulatory_change": []}, "links": {"pdf": [], "dataset": [], "related": []}, "celex_id": null, "call_id": null, "award_id": null, "tags": [], "dedupe_signature": "054d72e44c35ca4275fb1433fbbe69f0267f8be75e3c402fb4d6d2f227b002f3", "embeddings": null, "extraction_notes": null}
{"schema": "document.v2", "source_id": "eur-lex.europa.eu", "source_name": "EUR-Lex", "url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/collection/n-law/n-case-law.html", "canonical_url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/collection/n-law/n-case-law.html", "fetch_time": "2026-06-23T06:39:57.934198+00:00", "language": "en", "title": "National case-law", "published_date": "2026-06-23T06:39:56.508568+00:00", "updated_date": null, "doc_type": "Blog/News", "programme": ["Other/NA"], "finance_instrument": [], "stage": null, "actors": [], "tech_area": [], "monetary_values": [], "summary_150w": "Do you want to help improving EUR-Lex ? This is a list of experimental features that you can enable. These features are still under development; they are not fully tested, and might reduce EUR-Lex stability. Don't forget to give your feedback! This document is an excerpt from the EUR-Lex website\nEU law\nEU case-law\nOfficial Journal\nNational law and case-law\nInformation\nIn this section, you can find national case-law and national case-law references in the field of European Union law. They\n   are mainly from EU Member States, but also from non-EU countries (Iceland, Liechtenstein, Norway, Switzerland, and the United\n   Kingdom). Some of the documents in this collection are also referenced in the JURE collection of EUR-Lex. You will find these documents and references accompanied by a rich legal analysis and links to related information. The title of the case is only available in the original language of the judgment. Keywords are available in French and English. Bibliographic information and search functionalities are available in all official EU languages. The left-hand side of this page gives access to search tools. Search in national case-law redirects to an advanced search form that offers many options. Searches will be performed only within the remit of the “national\n         case-law” section. On the top of the search form, you can choose whether to include case-law summaries in the search results.\n\nReferences\n• Source — 23 Jun 2026 — https://eur-lex.europa.eu/collection/n-law/n-case-law.html", "key_points": [], "implications": {"innovation_direction": [], "capital_structure": [], "regulatory_change": []}, "links": {"pdf": [], "dataset": [], "related": []}, "celex_id": null, "call_id": null, "award_id": null, "tags": [], "dedupe_signature": "b9d936660e0640bc950c9a93f84e0e06f69d33c908ae473402fe4c27b765cade", "embeddings": null, "extraction_notes": null}
{"schema": "document.v2", "source_id": "eur-lex.europa.eu", "source_name": "EUR-Lex", "url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/collection/n-law/jure.html", "canonical_url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/collection/n-law/jure.html", "fetch_time": "2026-06-23T06:40:00.061637+00:00", "language": "en", "title": "JURE case-law", "published_date": "2026-06-23T06:39:58.396861+00:00", "updated_date": null, "doc_type": "Blog/News", "programme": ["Other/NA"], "finance_instrument": [], "stage": null, "actors": [], "tech_area": [], "monetary_values": [], "summary_150w": "Do you want to help improving EUR-Lex ? This is a list of experimental features that you can enable. These features are still under development; they are not fully tested, and might reduce EUR-Lex stability. Don't forget to give your feedback! This document is an excerpt from the EUR-Lex website\nEU law\nEU case-law\nOfficial Journal\nNational law and case-law\nInformation\nJURE stands for jurisdiction, recognition and enforcement of judgments in civil and\n   \n   commercial matters. In this section you can find relevant judgments on judicial cooperation in civil and commercial matters delivered by:\nJudgments by national courts are available in their original language only, but:\nThe left-hand side of this page gives access to search tools. More on JURE case-law Less on JURE case-law\nThe JURE case–law collection was created under Article 3 of Protocol 2 of the 2007 Lugano Convention . That article required the European Commission to set up a publicly accessible system\n      \n      containing relevant judgments delivered under that Convention and other instruments\n      \n      that have an influence on its application. Over time, the collection has been expanded and now contains judgments under the following:\n\nReferences\n• Source — 23 Jun 2026 — https://eur-lex.europa.eu/collection/n-law/jure.html", "key_points": [], "implications": {"innovation_direction": [], "capital_structure": [], "regulatory_change": []}, 